<p>It is possible to process the data from a {tag 'tag'} before it is used by PAD to construct the output.
<p>This is done by using one of the below options.
<p>dedup, end, first, group, last, page, random, reverse, row, rows, shuffle, slice, sort, splice, start, trim, where
<p>The options run in the order they are written. <code>where</code> keeps the rows a quoted expression holds for, evaluated per row with the row's fields; when the options leave no row at all, the tag shows its {construct 'else'} branch. <code>group</code> folds the rows into one occurrence per value of a field, with subtotals - see <a href="?pages/grouping">grouping with subtotals</a>.

